","statement":"DeleteSpaceMember is the assessed handler entry and first requires the current user.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-78bfbd739bb9ce65","startLine":740,"endLine":746}]},{"id":"om-identity-binding","kind":"binding","statement":"The handler binds the authenticated current user and passes that identity into resource resolution.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-78bfbd739bb9ce65","startLine":741,"endLine":746}]},{"id":"om-resource-binding","kind":"binding","statement":"Resource resolution binds the selected space, target user, caller membership, and target membership, requiring the target membership to be active before returning success.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-78bfbd739bb9ce65","startLine":632,"endLine":662}]},{"id":"om-active-condition","kind":"condition","statement":"The source defines an active member as having administrator or ordinary-user role.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-a1b44d1a06dae144","startLine":64,"endLine":66}]},{"id":"om-authorization-control","kind":"control","statement":"For a target other than the caller, the handler requires space-administrator authority on the caller membership.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-78bfbd739bb9ce65","startLine":750,"endLine":755}]},{"id":"om-protected-effect","kind":"effect","statement":"The membership deletion call and success publication occur only after the non-self authorization check succeeds.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-78bfbd739bb9ce65","startLine":756,"endLine":763}]}],"decisiveMissingFacts":[],"suggestedObservations":[]},{"obligationId":"scenario%3Aself-leave::entry%3Adelete-member","decision":{"kind":"observed","observed":"allow"},"branchResults":[],"explanation":"Source-visible behavior: the handler authenticates the caller, resolves the caller and target memberships, compares targetUser.ID with currentUser.ID, and skips the administrator gate when the target is the caller. Under the supplied premise that the active ordinary non-administrator caller targets their own active membership and resource resolution succeeds, the source reaches the protected Store.DeleteSpaceMember effect and then publishes the space change on store success. The accepted policy comparison is separate: policy:current allows an active ordinary member to delete their own membership, matching the source authorization path. A possible store error is source-external mutation behavior, not authorization; it does not change that the source permits the operation to reach the effect. The supplied entry and fixed crop establish this declared handler path only; source discovery is not-tested, so no repository-wide completeness or deployment conclusion is made.","facts":[{"id":"sl-entry","kind":"entry","statement":"DeleteSpaceMember is the assessed handler entry and first requires the current user.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-78bfbd739bb9ce65","startLine":740,"endLine":746}]},{"id":"sl-identity-binding","kind":"binding","statement":"The handler binds the authenticated current user and passes that identity into resource resolution.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-78bfbd739bb9ce65","startLine":741,"endLine":746}]},{"id":"sl-resource-binding","kind":"binding","statement":"Resource resolution binds the selected space, target user, caller membership, and target membership, requiring the target membership to be active before returning success.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-78bfbd739bb9ce65","startLine":632,"endLine":662}]},{"id":"sl-active-condition","kind":"condition","statement":"The source defines an active member as having administrator or ordinary-user role.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-a1b44d1a06dae144","startLine":64,"endLine":66}]},{"id":"sl-authorization-control","kind":"control","statement":"The administrator requirement is conditional on the target not being the caller; the self-target case bypasses that gate.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-78bfbd739bb9ce65","startLine":750,"endLine":755}]},{"id":"sl-protected-effect","kind":"effect","statement":"After authorization, the handl